title Eight tracks: eight audio tracks record onto the stick beside a demo song, play back from their files, two record while six play, then the project is saved and opened again
covers stream-record, stream-play, stream-record-while-playing, stream-seek, stream-save, stream-open
needs demo-songs, stream-audio
# D3 (docs/dev/design/disk-streaming.md): the whole app, with its takes on the
# stick. host_streamtest_mpc.py puts this run's data folder on partition 4,
# so every take is written there as it records and plays back from its file.
# The tracks record the line input (mono; silent with nothing plugged in): the
# drive does the same work either way. Each mark's status line (and one every
# 30 s) counts the takes on their files and how much went silent because the
# stick was late: tools/mpc-one/devtest_report.py puts them in its tables.
wait 2
mark open
button BROWSE
tap browser place Projects
tap browser row Night Market
tap browser row Night Market
wait 1
expect project: Night Market is in
mark tracks
tap header tab Arrange
tap clips song Song
tap song button Play song
expect time: song on
# Eight audio tracks, each armed as it is added.
tap song add-track + Track
tap song add-kind Audio track
wait 0.5
tap song add-track + Track
tap song add-kind Audio track
wait 0.5
tap song add-track + Track
tap song add-kind Audio track
wait 0.5
tap song add-track + Track
tap song add-kind Audio track
wait 0.5
tap song add-track + Track
tap song add-kind Audio track
wait 0.5
tap song add-track + Track
tap song add-kind Audio track
wait 0.5
tap song add-track + Track
tap song add-kind Audio track
wait 0.5
tap song add-track + Track
tap song add-kind Audio track
wait 0.5
expect time: Audio 8 added
# Two minutes of all eight recording while the song plays: twice the audio
# track memory, so each take's memory goes back as its file holds it.
mark record-eight
button REC
wait 0.5
button PLAY
wait 120
button STOP
wait 2
# The eight takes play back from their files, with the song.
mark play-eight
button PLAY START
wait 60
# Back to the start twice while it plays: the starts are held in the cache.
button PLAY START
wait 20
button PLAY START
wait 40
button STOP
wait 2
# Tracks 7 and 8 record again while 1 to 6 play from their files.
mark record-two
tap song arm Audio 1 arm
tap song arm Audio 2 arm
tap song arm Audio 3 arm
tap song arm Audio 4 arm
tap song arm Audio 5 arm
tap song arm Audio 6 arm
button REC
wait 0.5
button PLAY
wait 60
button STOP
wait 2
# The save copies every take's file into the project on the stick.
mark save
button SHIFT + BROWSE
wait 60
expect project: saved Night Market
# Opened again: the takes open on their files in the project's samples.
mark open-again
button BROWSE
tap browser place Projects
tap browser row Night Market
tap browser row Night Market
wait 10
expect project: Night Market is in
expect project: 8 audio tracks and 10 takes in
mark play-again
tap header tab Arrange
tap clips song Song
tap song button Play song
button PLAY START
wait 60
button STOP
wait 2
mark end
